Fuzzy-search the whole workspace from the composer's "@" menu.

Upstream's "@" menu browses one folder at a time: "@auth" only finds
auth.ts at the workspace root, and reaching a nested file means opening
each folder. Once the workspace's file index (server patch
0011-mention-file-index.patch) has loaded, typing a name now matches every
file and folder fzf-style, like Claude Code's and Codex's own pickers: the
characters must appear in order but not together, so "@srvts" finds
src/server.ts. Matches in the file name, at word and camel-case boundaries,
and in a row rank higher, files a little above folders, shorter paths
above longer ones. "@src/au" searches all of src. A bare "@" and "@<folder>/" still browse, so Enter on
a folder result opens it and Tab attaches it whole. Rows show the matched
characters in bold and the folder each result is in. Without the index
(still loading, or an older runner) the menu filters the folder as before.
The new-session launcher's "@" menu, which reads the host's filesystem, is
unchanged.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0013.

